      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hoplias_aimara_amapa_brazil_en/",
      "html": "<p>Hoplias aimara belongs to the fighters. Without any fear they attack even humans. H. aimara attains a length of more than one meter, so one should be really careful with these fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hoplias_aimara_amapa_brazil_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species has been known so far only from French Guyana and Venezuela. It has now been imported for the first time from the Brazilian state of Amapa.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hoplias_aimara_amapa_brazil_en/",
      "html": "<p>H. aimara differs from all other species of Hoplias by the very large eye. The specimens from Amapa are also much more colorful than any Hoplias seen so far.</p>"
    }
  ],
